      "rationale": "This unguarded equation defines the total summary symbol zeroResidueCount by the supplied Python-floor-division arithmetic expression; it names a mathematical result and does not perform or observe program execution.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-7f4fda07af964878549fb6179e4214215094e6afdc0f799801aef078770bc8f4",
      "start_line": 18,
      "text": "  rule zeroResidueCount(N)\n    => ((N +Int 1) -Int pyMod(N +Int 1, 3)) /Int 3"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 24,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "da6a4e2936c513bfd13e5a5dabe3f487b5f2fc80dad7975a6a8838c23f087590",
      "rationale": "This unguarded equation defines the total summary symbol chooseThree as X*(X-1)*(X-2)//6 in the reference semantics' pyMod and /Int normal form; it is a named arithmetic definition rather than an additional fact or operational rule.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-da6a4e2936c513bfd13e5a5dabe3f487b5f2fc80dad7975a6a8838c23f087590",
      "start_line": 22,
      "text": "  rule chooseThree(X)\n    => (X *Int (X -Int 1) *Int (X -Int 2)\n        -Int pyMod(X *Int (X -Int 1) *Int (X -Int 2), 6)) /Int 6"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 28,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "f0b13856a8dad7aae0ba7cb74d4c557bf3d05dd316341f9923211e2c0e60ee6c",
      "rationale": "This unguarded equation defines expectedTriples by composing zeroResidueCount and chooseThree into the two-case combinatorial sum used by the postcondition; it introduces the named proof term without replacing execution.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-f0b13856a8dad7aae0ba7cb74d4c557bf3d05dd316341f9923211e2c0e60ee6c",
      "start_line": 26,
      "text": "  rule expectedTriples(N)\n    => chooseThree(zeroResidueCount(N))\n       +Int chooseThree(N -Int zeroResidueCount(N))"
    }
  ],
